## 🛠️ Design & Mechanics

               ┌─────────────────────────┐
               │ Top Joint: Tilt Sensor  │ (Contains rolling ball switch)
               └────┬───────────────┬────┘
                    │               │
             (+) Positive       (-) Negative
                Wire            Wire
                    │               │
                    ▼               ▼
               ┌─────────────────────────┐
               │ Side Loop: Micro Buzzer │ (Mounted on outer ear frame)
               └────┬───────────────┬────┘
                    │               │
                    └──────[ Battery ]┘ (Powers the loop)
1.Hearing-Aid Form Factor: The casing hooks over the top of the ear to keep it lightweight, stable, and ergonomic.

2.Top Joint (Tilt Switch): A mechanical tilt sensor housing a small conductive metal ball is positioned at the top joint of the frame.

3.Trigger Mechanism: While driving with proper posture, the circuit remains OPEN. When sleepiness causes the head to nod forward, gravity pulls the metal ball to the front of the sensor, bridging the internal contacts to CLOSE the circuit.

4.Side Loop (Alert Buzzer): Closing the loop immediately routes power to the piezo buzzer on the side of the casing, delivering a loud sound next to the driver's ear to instantly wake them up.

CIRCUIT DIAGRAM:
[ Power Source (+) ] ───> [ Top Joint: Tilt Sensor ] ───> [ Side Loop: Buzzer ] ───> [ Ground / Battery (-) ]

COMPONENTS:
Tilt Sensor: Mechanical ball-type switch.

Alert Unit: Miniature 3V/5V Piezo Buzzer.

Power Source: Compact button cell battery.

Frame: Custom behind-the-ear casing & connecting wires.
